            <div xml:id="d248">

                <pb facs="0236" n="224" sameAs="frus:frus1943v04/pg224"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">845.00/1981: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Officer in Charge at New Delhi</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Merrell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">New Delhi</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-06-15T15:00:00+06:30">June 15, 1943—3
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 16—3:42 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>403. Nehru’s sister, Mrs. Pandit, and his daughter Mrs. Indira Gandhi who were
                    ill are reported to have been released unconditionally from jail.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Merrell</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
